# Workflow plan step D1 (docs/WORKFLOW_PLAN.md, 2026-11-14): DEME Setup in layers. The physical setup first (the grains, the
# material and its presets, gravity, the box, the times); the numerical choices (time step, softened stiffness, search speed,
# output frames ...) behind Advanced, with a line saying what they amount to, and each one with what it changes.
action go.new
wait-until page New case
click new-prog:deme
wait 5
click label:Settle a bed
wait 5
click clone-name
key A ctrl
type d1bed
click clone-go
wait-until page Overview timeout 10
click nav:setup
wait-until page Setup
wait 10
assert text Advanced: the numerical choices
assert text They make the run feasible on a GPU
assert text Material preset
assert not text The step the contacts are integrated with
screenshot $OUT/d1_closed.png
click dm-advanced
wait 5
assert text The step the contacts are integrated with
assert text The fastest a grain may go
screenshot $OUT/d1_open.png
